---
/**
 * Starlight's ThemeProvider, replaced so the theme rule is GMT's (plan #266, D3; #352, D4). Starlight's own looks for a
 * `<select>` and a `#theme-icons` template to update the control; this site's control is the "Dark theme" switch in the
 * settings panel (SettingsControl.astro), which `src/lib/settings-control.ts` keeps in step, so there is nothing for the
 * provider to draw. (Until #352 the control was a two-state button whose icon this provider drew.)
 *
 * Ported from GMT, apps/dox/src/components/ThemeProvider.astro at commit b15b3899 (its Earth-look lines are left out).
 * The script is inline on purpose: it sets `data-theme` before first paint, so there is no flash of the wrong theme,
 * and it cannot import. Its storage rule is the one in src/lib/theme.ts (`readTheme`): key `starlight-theme`, only
 * "light" or "dark" is a stored theme, anything else follows the system. Change both together.
 * `updatePickers` stays as a no-op because Starlight's Page.astro may call it.
 */
---

{/* This is intentionally inlined to avoid FOUC. */}
<script is:inline>
  window.StarlightThemeProvider = (() => {
    const storageKey = 'starlight-theme';
    const stored =
      typeof localStorage !== 'undefined' && localStorage.getItem(storageKey);
    const theme =
      stored === 'light' || stored === 'dark'
        ? stored
        : window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches
          ? 'light'
          : 'dark';
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
    return {
      updatePickers() {},
    };
  })();
</script>
